  {
    "@id": "https://www.allbodiesdance.ca/events-1/on-display-global",
    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "On Display Global | All Bodies Dance"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>PERFORMANCE OPPORTUNITY:</strong> <strong>ON DISPLAY GLOBAL</strong>   Sunday December 3, 2023 (in person and online)</p>\n<p>You are invited to take part in<a rel=\"noopener noreferrer noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://allbodiesdance.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u&#61;14a061660369bf8dffcb7c145&amp;id&#61;94879b65a9&amp;e&#61;981f760f7b\"> </a>ON DISPLAY GLOBAL (ODG), a performance taking place both in person and online on Sunday, December 3 in honour of<a rel=\"noopener noreferrer noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://allbodiesdance.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u&#61;14a061660369bf8dffcb7c145&amp;id&#61;1c98abd288&amp;e&#61;981f760f7b\"> </a>United Nations’ International Day of Persons with Disabilities.</p>\n<p><strong>WHAT IS ON DISPLAY GLOBAL?</strong></p>\n<p>ODG is an annual, worldwide initiative led by New York based Heidi Latsky Dance . It is an in-person and virtual event lasting 24 hours and streamed live on Zoom. Part meditation and part art exhibition, participants move almost imperceptibly slowly for the entire performance, (while also taking care of themselves of course as we do in ABDP!) There are no grand gestures or big movements. The performance invites dancers of all ages, sizes, and embodiments to be “on display” as “sculptures”. The piece is a “commentary on the body as spectacle and society&#39;s obsession with body image.”</p>\n<p><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://allbodiesdance.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u&#61;14a061660369bf8dffcb7c145&amp;id&#61;07b276a0aa&amp;e&#61;981f760f7b\"><strong>Click here to learn more.</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong>WHERE AND WHEN DOES ODG TAKE PLACE?</strong></p>\n<p>This year, dancers can participate in-person or online but they must take part in the rehearsal to learn the performance score.</p>\n<p><u><strong>In-person</strong></u><strong>  Rehearsal</strong></p>\n<p>Sunday November 26, 11 to 1 pm PST</p>\n<p>Scotiabank Dance Centre, 677 Davie St</p>\n<p>3rd floor studio</p>\n<p><strong>Performance</strong></p>\n<p>Sunday December 3, 1:00 to 2:00 pm PST</p>\n<p>Trout Lake Community Centre lobby</p>\n<p>We will perform “pop-up” style in the lobby at the Trout Lake Community Centre. Our &#34;sculpture court&#34; will be set up in and among the public in the community centre.</p>\n<p><u><strong>Online</strong></u><strong>  Rehearsal</strong></p>\n<p>Heidi Latsky Dance online training sessions:</p>\n<p>Sunday November 12th at 12pm EST</p>\n<p>Tuesday November 14th at 12pm EST</p>\n<p>Sunday November 19th at 5pm EST</p>\n<p>Tuesday November 28th at 12pm EST</p>\n<p><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://allbodiesdance.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u&#61;14a061660369bf8dffcb7c145&amp;id&#61;3c41a48d05&amp;e&#61;981f760f7b\"><strong>Register to receive the link</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong>Performance</strong></p>\n<p>Sunday December 3, time to be confirmed soon (please contact us for more info)</p>\n<p>Zoom from your home</p>\n<p><strong>REQUIREMENTS TO PARTICIPATE</strong></p>\n<p>1. Email <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://mailto:info&#64;allbodiesdance.ca/\">info&#64;allbodiesdance.ca</a> by Monday November 20, 2023 and tell us if you will be participating online or in-person.</p>\n<p>2. Attend the in person rehearsal on Sunday November 26 from 11 to 1pm  or attend one of the online meetings prior to Dec 3, 2023</p>\n<p>3. If you need ASL interpretation for the in person rehearsal and performance email us by Sunday November 19 at the latest.</p>\n<p>4. Find a costume of all white clothing for the performance.</p>"
      }
    ],
